    "id": "cartoon-09",
    "title": "David Bravo (Honys Torres, 2021)",
    "category": "Cartoon",
    "description": "“David Bravo” opens the series Monumentos Lúdicos as an act of appropriation and critical irreverence toward the history of the idealized body. The work merges Michelangelo’s canonical David with the cartoon figure Johnny Bravo, confronting the classical ideal with contemporary pop narcissism. This collision exposes the ongoing construction of male perfection—from Renaissance marble to animated exaggeration—and reveals how bodies are shaped by cultural myths, pressures, and fantasies. Through sharp humor and symbolic precision, the piece dismantles the authority of the monument and reframes the body as a site of irony, tension, and visual freedom. Technical details: David Bravo, 2021. Acrylic on canvas. 60 × 50 cm. Honys Torres.",
