    "id": "cartoon-13",
    "title": "Karl (2024) – Acrylic on Canvas by Honys Torres",
    "category": "Cartoon",
    "description": "“Karl” (2024) is a Neo Pop artwork by Venezuelan artist Honys Torres, created as part of the Zürich POP collection. The central LEGO‑style figure represents Karl der Grosse (Charlemagne), referencing the medieval legend that attributes the founding of the Grossmünster to him. Behind the figure appears the stylized façade of the Grossmünster, one of Zürich’s most iconic landmarks and a symbol deeply tied to the city’s historical identity. Torres blends this legendary reference with cartoon characters, playful doodles, multilingual greetings, and pop‑culture elements, creating a vibrant reinterpretation of Zürich’s cultural mythology. The work reflects her interest in urban identity, historical narratives, and the fusion of local heritage with contemporary pop iconography. Medium: Acrylic on canvas Dimensions: 70 × 70 cm Year: 2024",
    "image": "/wallpapers/curated/cartoon-13.jpg",
    "premium": false,
