    "description": "“Happy Pride” (2024) is a Neo Pop artwork by Venezuelan artist Honys Torres, created as part of the Zürich POP collection. The piece portrays a joyful Pride celebration in Zürich, with LEGO‑style unicorn figures waving rainbow flags in a vibrant, festive atmosphere. In the background appears the Pavillon at Bürkliplatz, an emblematic lakeside structure that anchors the scene in one of the city’s most recognizable public spaces. Torres blends LGBTQ+ symbolism, cartoon characters, multilingual greetings, and pop‑culture elements to create a dynamic tribute to diversity, inclusion, and urban community life. The work reflects her interest in collective identity, celebration, and the playful reinterpretation of Zürich’s cultural landmarks. Medium: Acrylic on canvas Dimensions: 70 × 70 cm Year: 2024",
