    "id": "cartoon-20",
    "title": "Le Corbusier (2024) – Acrylic on Canvas by Honys Torres",
    "category": "Cartoon",
    "description": "“Le Corbusier” (2024) is a Neo Pop artwork by Venezuelan artist Honys Torres, created as part of the Zürich POP collection. The central LEGO‑style figure represents Le Corbusier, one of the most influential architects of the 20th century, known for his radical modernist vision and his signature round glasses. In the background appears the Pavillon Le Corbusier in Zürich, the architect’s final building and a landmark of Swiss modern architecture. Completed in 1967, the pavilion embodies Le Corbusier’s principles of modularity, color, and structural clarity, combining steel, glass, and enamel panels in a sculptural composition. Torres reinterprets this architectural icon through a vibrant pop‑culture lens, blending cartoon characters, bold colors, and graffiti‑inspired elements to create a playful dialogue between architectural heritage and contemporary visual culture. The work reflects her interest in urban identity, modernist symbolism, and the reinterpretation of Zürich’s cultural landmarks through Neo Pop aesthetics. Medium: Acrylic on canvas Dimensions: 70 × 70 cm Year: 2024",
